###Text
Text test::borealprairie2::text::HandlingOverview
{
  type: markdown;
  content: '# Prairie Grain Handling Register\n\nEvery movement of grain through the terminal is recorded once, against the specialisation that matches how the grain moved.\n\n* **Intake** — grain arriving from a hauler, graded on arrival and optionally tied to a moisture sample.\n* **Outload** — grain leaving a bin into railcars for an onward terminal.\n* **Transfer** — grain moved between two bins; the aerated form additionally records fan run hours and the moisture the transfer was aiming for.\n\nThe supertype carries only what is true of all three: the movement code, the date it was recorded, the net tonnes and the crop. Reporting reads the supertype and narrows to a specialisation only when the extra fields are needed.\n';
}
